{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>You shall not lend on interest to your brother.</b> After warning to guard against the things that cause the Shekhinah to depart from Israel, he warned concerning the kinds of kindness that cause it to dwell among Israel. These are the matter of interest and vows, from which comes charity one is obligated to give promptly, as the poor are frequently encountered (Rosh Hashanah 6a), and the matter of a hired worker's food (Deuteronomy 23:25), and the matter of the bill of divorce (Deuteronomy 24:1), which should not be given except on account of ervat davar (a matter of indecency), to remove every stumbling block of mamzerut, not otherwise, as it says: כי ה׳ העיד בינך ובין אשת נעוריך אשר אתה בגדתה (Malachi 2:14). And the kindness to a new wife — ושמח את אשתו (Deuteronomy 24:5). And the kindness: לא יחבול רחים ורכב (Deuteronomy 24:6). And the guard against public harmers — man-stealers (Deuteronomy 24:7) who are found to steal children. And the guard in the matter of tzara'at (Deuteronomy 24:8), to isolate the metzora'im so that their tzara'at not cause harm by contact. And guarding against talebearing and slander (Deuteronomy 24:9). And the kindness to the borrower, the hired laborer, and the poor regarding the gleanings (Deuteronomy 24:19). And compassion on the one flogged (Deuteronomy 25:3) and on the animal in threshing (Deuteronomy 25:4), and on the dead man without seed, that his name not be blotted out (Deuteronomy 25:5)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The Talmudic citation שכיחי עניים (Rosh Hashanah 6a) is given in Aramaic; rendered into English as Sforno quotes it, with the reference normalized. The legal terms ervat davar and mamzerut are standard halakhic categories and left untranslated as technical terms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:07.476455896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}